\">As of Oct 12, the record for Hancock County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, April to May hit 174% of normal and November to December fell to 39%. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 15787 at 55%.</p>"}
